WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.585
Every BxAgents project can ship its own chat page.

00:00:03.905 --> 00:00:08.364
This is the web UI of an Acme support agent, built from one gateway file.

00:00:08.684 --> 00:00:11.607
It starts at sign in, with accounts you declare in code.

00:00:12.206 --> 00:00:14.318
Signed in, you land in a clean chat.

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:21.017
The header shows the agent and its controls: your conversations, the model picker, notes, an API key, and the theme.

00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:26.629
Ask a question and the answer streams in as it is written, with Markdown formatting and lists.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.906
The model picker lists the profiles the app chose to offer.

00:00:33.226 --> 00:00:38.517
Pick the planner profile, and the next answer comes from a different model, in the same conversation.

00:00:39.116 --> 00:00:45.324
When the agent calls a tool, the page shows it as a block you can open, with the tool's name and what it was called with.

00:00:45.925 --> 00:00:47.738
Every conversation is saved.

00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:51.920
Start a new chat, and the old one stays in the list, ready to open again.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:55.165
Notes keep what the agent should remember about you.

00:00:55.485 --> 00:00:57.448
Add one, and it is there next time.

00:00:58.048 --> 00:01:01.312
Dark mode is one click, and the page remembers your choice.

00:01:01.911 --> 00:01:09.186
That is the whole web UI: sign in, streaming answers, a model picker you control, tools, saved conversations, notes and themes.

00:01:09.506 --> 00:01:12.386
All from a few lines of YAML and one gateway file.

